urposes. First and foremost, it blocks Black\'s diagonal Open 3 (F8-G7-H6), preventing an immediate loss. Secondly, placing a White stone at I5 connects with the existing White stones at G5 and H5 to form a White Open 3 (G5-H5-I5). This move is a "Sente" move (a move that retains initiative), as it forces Black to respond to White\'s new threat (likely by blocking at J5 or F5), rather than allowing Black to develop new attacks. Blocking at E9 would stop the Black threat but is passive and does not create a counter-threat for White. Therefore, I5 is the optimal move.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 5}'}
